# Python virtual environment (Windows)

This repo uses a local venv at `.venv/`. Do not install packages into the system/user Python.

A `beforeShellExecution` hook (`.cursor/hooks/venv-guard.ps1`) also prompts when bare `pip install` or `python main.py` would bypass the venv.

## Shell commands

Before `pip`, `python`, `pytest`, or running `main.py`:

1. Prefer the venv interpreter directly (works without activating):
   - `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe`
   - `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt`
2. Or activate first: `.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1`

## Rules

- If `.venv` is missing, create it: `python -m venv .venv`, then `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt`.
- Never run bare `pip install` or `python -m pip install` without the venv path unless the user explicitly asks for a global install.
- New dependencies go in `requirements.txt`; install only via `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt`.
- For this project, set `PYTHONPATH=src` when running CLI (e.g. `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py`).

## Examples

```powershell
# Good
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
$env:PYTHONPATH="src"; .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe main.py --crawler fred
# or: .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m macromind.db.migrate  (pytest picks up src/ via pyproject.toml)

# Bad
pip install httpx
python main.py --crawler fred
```
